{
  "info": {
    "name": "Mountain Hut - E2E change booking",
    "description": "End-to-end scenario for MH-06 (change a booking), run against the real running server.\n\nA hiker books a slot and then changes the party size, the requirements and the slot; the refused changes (a date without a time, no free seats, a missing booking, someone else's booking, a warden, less than 48 hours before the slot) leave the booking as it was.\n\nStart the server on a freshly seeded db, from the backend folder, for example:\n\n    DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////tmp/mh_e2e.db SEED_DATA=true fastapi dev app/main.py\n\nThen run the collection in order with the Collection Runner or:\n\n    newman run MH_E2E_change_booking.postman_collection.json\n\nThe collection needs two slots that start more than 72 hours from now (the seed creates slots for the following days). Every run registers new hikers with unique emails and the 48 hours scenario creates its own slot, so it can be repeated on the same db until the last slot is full (each run puts a party of four on it, about ten runs): then restart the server on a freshly seeded db.\nThe email sent after a change is not checked here: Postman cannot read the mailbox, see the integration tests.\nThe warden is the seeded one (luca.bonetti@rifugio.example).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "slotADate",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "slotATime",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "slotBDate",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "slotBTime",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "bookingId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "tableA",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "tableB",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "closeStart",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "closeEnd",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "closeSlotId",
